timestamp=2026-11-04T16:16:01.771Z level=INFO run=4cbc268f message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us also look at other potential spoilage indicators. For example, \"spoiled\" goods might have patterns in weights? \n# Compare total_weight_kg in dispatches to quantity * unit_weight_kg from catalog. \n# If there was spoilage, sometimes weight changes, but not stated. Or maybe frozen products partially thawed? Less likely to show in recorded weights exactly. Let us check the 03:17 dispatch weights.\nimport csv\n\ncatalog = {}\nwith open('/app/dataset/product_catalog.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        pid = row['product_id']\n        ean = row['ean_code']\n        w = float(row['unit_weight_kg'].replace(',', '.'))\n        catalog[pid] = w\n        catalog[ean] = w\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/warehouse_dispatches.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        if '2023-07-18 03:17' in row['timestamp']:\n            pid = row['product_id']\n            qty = int(row['quantity'])\n            w = float(row['total_weight_kg'])\n            cw = catalog.get(pid)\n            if cw:\n                print(pid, qty, 'expected', qty*cw, 'got', w)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
